  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened capacity of member States to ratify and apply international labour standards and to fulfil their reporting obligations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Grenada has been facing challenges in meeting its reporting obligations as an ILO member State. To address this, the ILO is assisting the Ministry of Legal Affairs, Labour and Consumer Affairs (MLLCA) with its reporting duties. This assistance is being provided mainly through training activities
 
Beneficiaries of this initiative include all employers and workers, who will benefit from legal protections improved by incorporating the results of dialogue with the ILO&apos;s supervisory mechanisms. The work will be done in collaboration with the MLLCA and the Labour Advisory Board. The ILO will provide legal and technical advisory services to support so that the country meets its reporting obligations.</narrative>
  </description>
